WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.530
- [Interviewer] All right, Shane?

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:04.370
- Yes, sir.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.380
- [Interviewer] Shane,
where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.213
Where are you from originally?

00:00:06.213 --> 00:00:07.793
- Mingo County, West Virginia.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.160
- [Interviewer] And tell
me about your childhood.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.660
You had both your parents
when you were a kid?

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.240
- Yes, I have both my parents.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.211
My mother was a hard worker,

00:00:14.211 --> 00:00:16.670
my father was an alcoholic.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.816
But my father died when I was
15, from drugs and alcohol-

00:00:20.816 --> 00:00:21.649
- [Interviewer] I'm sorry.

00:00:21.649 --> 00:00:22.490
- It's okay.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:24.893
And that just put a big
ole hole in my world.

00:00:26.807 --> 00:00:29.300
Everything negative, it made
in my whole life negative.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.840
Everything, I just fed into that.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.443
I become a drug addict like that.

00:00:33.443 --> 00:00:35.280
- [Interviewer] Is that when
drug use started for you?

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.933
- Yes, sir.

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:37.882
- [Interviewer] And you
guys were very poor?

00:00:37.882 --> 00:00:39.033
- Oh, very poor.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.580
My mom was a CNA, which they
make like 10, $11 an hour.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.910
And that's what we lived off of.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:44.743
- [Interviewer] How many kids?

00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:45.576
- Five.

00:00:45.576 --> 00:00:46.420
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.653
- Four boys and a girl.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.010
- [Interviewer] How far
did you go in school?

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:50.843
- To 11th grade.

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:52.713
Well, midway through the 11th.

00:00:55.756 --> 00:00:58.660
- [Interviewer] Where'd
your life go after that?

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.220
- Nowhere, I became a drug addict.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.260
Then by the time I'm 20, I'm locked up.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.450
I'm 33 right now, just got off.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.150
Just got released today.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.500
- [Interviewer] How many
years were you in prison?

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.743
- Seven straight.

00:01:10.743 --> 00:01:12.225
- [Interviewer] Seven straight years?

00:01:12.225 --> 00:01:13.530
- Seven straight years.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:16.460
- [Interviewer] Wow, did those seven years

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.650
change you in any way?

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:18.483
- Yeah, they did.

00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:19.700
They made me grow up a lot.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:22.080
Made me stop taking
everything for granted,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.134
and realize that life does go on.

00:01:26.134 --> 00:01:28.770
While I was in prison though,

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:32.543
I had to have that GED
class to make a job, right.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:36.240
I would go to GED class and
I would sleep every day.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.410
And the teacher, he came back there

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.260
and he woke me up one day.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.210
He's an old man.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.970
He said, he called me boy.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.930
And he said, "Boy, won't you do me a favor

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.025
and make your GED, man."

00:01:45.025 --> 00:01:46.080
He said, "You're a smart kid."

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.368
He said, "I'm getting ready
to retire in six months."

00:01:48.368 --> 00:01:50.230
He said, "If you don't make the GED,

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:51.110
you're going to be stuck here.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.910
And it's just a hell hole."

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:54.990
It's Huttonsville West
Virginia Penitentiary.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:59.793
It's like top notch Guantanamo Bay shit.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.130
And so I took him serious
and I went back the next day.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.230
I said, "Denny, you know what?

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.110
I'm gonna try and make my GED."

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.560
So I made my GED in 63 days.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.066
And I made it with a 3,174 score,

00:02:11.066 --> 00:02:14.053
which is a scholarship
anywhere in America.

00:02:15.179 --> 00:02:16.850
I've not pursued it though,

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:19.800
but I did make my GED
and I did become a man.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.850
When I got out, I went to Texas.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:24.523
I found a nurse, she's never been high.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.017
We've been together for two years now,

00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:30.253
and we have a four month
old son, doing good.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.160
- [Interviewer] How were you together?

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.920
You were in prison? But you were with her?

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.720
- No, I met her from in prison.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:36.553
- [Interviewer] Oh, I see.

00:02:36.553 --> 00:02:37.386
- My sister lives in Texas.

00:02:37.386 --> 00:02:38.219
- [Interviewer] You were dating her

00:02:38.219 --> 00:02:39.052
while you were in prison.

00:02:39.052 --> 00:02:39.885
- I talked to her.

00:02:39.885 --> 00:02:40.718
We didn't date, we just talked-

00:02:40.718 --> 00:02:42.099
- [Interviewer] Yeah, that's what I mean.

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:43.051
- (indistinct) I shook
her hand when I met her,

00:02:43.051 --> 00:02:45.053
it was a whole new vibe.

00:02:45.053 --> 00:02:46.730
(interviewer laughs)

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.123
She's a blessing, her
name is Rocio Bocanegra.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.330
I'm trying to have another baby with her,

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.814
as soon as I go home.

00:02:53.814 --> 00:02:55.519
- [Interviewer] What are you
gonna do with your life now,

00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:57.100
you've been out for one day.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.990
- Yes, I want to go to Texas,

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.536
and I'm gonna go to work for
this construction company

00:03:01.536 --> 00:03:05.470
where I redo the piers on the
freeways, the concrete drains.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:08.470
And I'm going to start my own
pressure washing business,

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:10.382
once I can get there, where
I go around to these car lots

00:03:10.382 --> 00:03:12.700
that have all these cars.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:15.613
I say, "Sir, I'll wash
your cars once a week

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:18.490
for $2 a car, wash them and dry them."

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:20.323
That's my goal.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.849
So hopefully I get it.

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:23.719
- [Interviewer] But you were telling me

00:03:23.719 --> 00:03:25.340
about being a pastor.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.965
- Yes. That's gonna be on my free time.

00:03:27.965 --> 00:03:30.499
I'm going to become a pastor.

00:03:30.499 --> 00:03:32.670
I got arrested on the church steps.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.230
I fell asleep on a porch,
praying for my wife and my son.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.690
I got so tired I couldn't move.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:37.780
I fall asleep and I wake up,

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.270
and the police is standing
over me with a flashlight.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:41.620
- [Interviewer] This is
what you got arrested for?

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.580
- No, they thought I was dead.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:43.980
This is how they brought me back here.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:44.813
- [Interviewer] Oh, I see.

00:03:44.813 --> 00:03:45.769
- On my parole.

00:03:45.769 --> 00:03:48.237
But yeah, I'm gonna become a pastor.

00:03:48.237 --> 00:03:49.729
Here's what I said.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.120
I said, I wanna become a pastor

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.510
and see what it takes to become a football

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.480
and basketball coach.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.670
Because once I got in prison,

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.810
I realized I was really good at sports.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.020
Like I would go months

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.110
and be the only white person on any team.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.470
And they have real leagues in there.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.730
They keep stats.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:05.879
I won two championships.

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:07.820
It's not a lot but it's amazing

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.318
because they give you fresh favorites,

00:04:09.318 --> 00:04:11.453
which is burger from the street.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.732
I was good.

00:04:13.732 --> 00:04:14.920
And I want to become a coach out there

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.230
and there's plenty of opportunities,

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.720
but I want to become a pastor

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.140
at this church Legacy
where I got arrested at.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.070
I went there, me and my
wife had been bickering

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.380
because me smoking marijuana,

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.025
she didn't agree with it.

00:04:27.025 --> 00:04:30.180
I hadn't seen my son all day.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.290
So I went to that church that
evening and I started praying.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.660
I said, "God, please give me my son.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.090
What I gotta do to get my son?

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.130
I want my family."

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.580
I just want to be a family...
That's all I ever wanted.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:40.760
I got so tired, I couldn't move.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.180
I fall asleep.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.740
I wake up and the cop standing over me.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.420
He arrest me and brings me back here.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.920
So I'm going to that church
to give him that testimony

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.556
and see what it takes to
become a pastor there.

00:04:51.556 --> 00:04:52.510
- [Interviewer] Good for you.

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:53.343
- God's like...

00:04:53.343 --> 00:04:55.985
He's gave me a whole new life out there.

00:04:55.985 --> 00:04:57.978
They are trying to build
us a new house now,

00:04:57.978 --> 00:04:59.623
habitat for humanity?

00:05:01.147 --> 00:05:04.510
I got a whole new blessing,
a whole new life ahead of me.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.440
The kid I was I don't have to be anymore.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:10.190
I became a man, I don't have
to worry about my dad anymore.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.010
because I get to be a dad.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:12.843
- [Interviewer] That's great.

00:05:12.843 --> 00:05:14.010
- Something I never could have did here.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:17.145
There's nothing here,
but drugs and dope hoes.

00:05:17.145 --> 00:05:19.320
You know anything about them?

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:20.773
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
everyone I've talked to is-

00:05:20.773 --> 00:05:23.170
- I went out there and
found a real woman, man.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.000
She's a hospice nurse.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:25.833
It's a blessing.

00:05:27.674 --> 00:05:29.910
My mom lives out there now,

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.630
we got a whole new life ahead of us.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.028
And I just keep praying to get there

00:05:34.028 --> 00:05:35.823
to take advantage of it.

00:05:38.855 --> 00:05:40.800
- [Interviewer] You
got money to get there?

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.100
- No, I'm waiting on them
to Money Gram me money.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.480
- [Interviewer] How much
you need to get there?

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.300
- The bus tickets $118

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.583
- [Interviewer] I'll take care of that.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:54.200
- I called them from the store
over here, just awhile ago

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.850
and they're probably
running wild right now

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:57.990
trying to get me there.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.110
- [Interviewer] Yeah, I'll help you out.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:05:59.943
- Thank you.

00:05:59.943 --> 00:06:01.550
- [Interviewer] Show me
what you showed me earlier.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:04.330
Those two pieces of styrofoam
that you wrote in prison.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.020
- Yeah, this is from dinner trays,

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:07.644
where they feed you, trays in the jail.

00:06:07.644 --> 00:06:09.735
And this is Bible verses.

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:10.875
Can I read them?

00:06:10.875 --> 00:06:12.162
- [Interviewer] Please.

00:06:12.162 --> 00:06:14.570
- This is Jeremiah 29 11 it says,

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:17.730
for I know the plans I have
for you, declares the Lord.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.400
Plans for welfare not for evil,

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.560
to give you a future and a hope.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.700
Jeremiah 33 verse three says,

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:25.380
call on to me and I will answer you

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:26.950
and tell you great and hidden things

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:28.380
that you have not known.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.604
Then Psalms 41 says, verse one,

00:06:31.604 --> 00:06:33.426
blessed is the one who considers the poor

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:37.020
in the day of trouble,
the Lord delivers him.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.610
And then John ten two says,

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.224
but he who enters by the door,

00:06:40.224 --> 00:06:42.950
is the shepherd of the sheep.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.100
And then Romans five one says,

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.188
therefore, since we have
been justified by faith

00:06:47.188 --> 00:06:50.260
we have peace with God
through our Lord Jesus Christ.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.156
But here's the best one ever.

00:06:51.156 --> 00:06:53.250
It's Romans 10, 10 it says,

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.160
brother my heart's desire and prayer

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.503
to God is that we all may be saved.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:04.070
And then this is my goals, I
was writing down for out there.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:07.520
It says looking to start my own business.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.980
Take half the money it grosses in a month

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.520
and start a trust fund for my son.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.150
Get my job back at WS Construction,

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:18.850
marry my wife as soon as possible.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:22.880
Be the best dad possible,
and have another baby.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.460
And enjoy life, don't have to look

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.260
over my shoulder anymore.

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:29.075
Get me a race car and get to having fun.

00:07:29.075 --> 00:07:32.170
Be moved in my own house by Thanksgiving,

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:35.350
so we can have Thanksgiving
dinner at my house.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.512
Take my wife on a cruise shortly somehow,

00:07:38.512 --> 00:07:41.530
and wake up Christmas
with Rocio and Chase,

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:42.402
is my wife and my son,

00:07:42.402 --> 00:07:45.043
just would be the best Christmas ever.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:50.930
And then phase two says,
make every plan work out.

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:54.610
Don't get frustrated and give
God time to fulfill it all.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:55.784
Find time to become a coach

00:07:55.784 --> 00:07:58.750
for football and basketball.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.220
Become a pastor preferably at Legacy

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:03.070
and enjoy the rest of
my life being humble,

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:05.290
kind and grateful and blessed.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:09.140
And knowing that every
sinner has a future,

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.833
and every saint has a past.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:16.463
- [Interviewer] That's beautiful.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:18.790
Thank you for sharing that.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.022
- You're Welcome.

00:08:20.022 --> 00:08:22.419
- [Interviewer] What got you
into prison in the first place?

00:08:22.419 --> 00:08:23.413
- Armed robbery.

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:29.580
I was on Oxycontin's and I woke up July 13

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:32.090
and I didn't have any money.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:35.330
And I went and robbed the store for $500.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:37.575
And they gave me 30 years
for robbing a store.

00:08:37.575 --> 00:08:38.560
- [Interviewer] 30 years?

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.500
Yes, and they used my
brother to testify on me.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.357
He worked for that store.

00:08:43.357 --> 00:08:44.830
- [Interviewer] Your brother
testified against you-

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.210
- Yes. And then while I'm in prison,

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:50.470
he robbed the same store for $10,000.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:52.440
And they only gave him one to three years,

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.873
which is 18 months.

00:08:54.783 --> 00:08:56.730
It just broke me down.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.410
I watched him come and leave,

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.930
while I'm there for the same
thing that he told on me for.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.750
But I forgive him, that's my brother.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.599
And he taught me how to tie my shoes.

00:09:05.599 --> 00:09:07.073
I can never hold it against him,

00:09:07.073 --> 00:09:09.850
because it's drugs, it's the devil.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:12.400
- [Interviewer] Do you think the pain

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.220
that you felt from that,

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.230
watching your brother come
and go for something worse,

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:19.706
and you getting punished
unfairly, perhaps.

00:09:19.706 --> 00:09:22.610
Do you think the pain that you felt

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:24.670
is what's gotten you
to where you are today?

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:26.748
- Yes, it gave me the
drive to never give up.

00:09:26.748 --> 00:09:30.063
It makes me understand that I'm tough.

00:09:30.063 --> 00:09:33.520
Because I was dependent on all of them,

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:35.374
I never really had a job or anything.

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:38.740
All I did was get high and this showed me

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.240
that I can count on myself.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:44.300
And it made me just
drive harder every day,

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.620
whatever I was doing, I wanna win at it.

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:49.257
Because I feel like I lose at everything.

00:09:49.257 --> 00:09:51.010
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
I've heard so many stories

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:51.843
in Appalachia...

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:57.070
From people who have gone
through extreme adversity.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:59.457
Everything about living in
Appalachia is difficult-

00:09:59.457 --> 00:10:00.290
- It's hard.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.230
- [Interviewer] From just
carrying your groceries

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:03.020
into the house is difficult
because every step

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:04.261
is up a steep hill or-

00:10:04.261 --> 00:10:05.410
- It's a stepping stone-

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.230
- [Interviewer] Yeah, It's
just a very difficult life

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:09.930
for many different reasons.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:11.750
And it seems like the people are...

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:19.480
They're just so kind and
compassionate and strong and-

00:10:20.766 --> 00:10:22.853
- They are, they're very strong-willed-

00:10:22.853 --> 00:10:23.686
- [Interviewer] And modest-

00:10:23.686 --> 00:10:25.020
- And they're very
honest, they don't have-

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.810
- [Interviewer] I've given
money to so many people here

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.372
that I've interviewed and
they just jumped back.

00:10:28.372 --> 00:10:30.283
They won't accept it.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:34.345
I gave a man a hundred bucks yesterday

00:10:34.345 --> 00:10:36.460
for talking with me
and he just jumped back

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:38.140
like, what are you doing?-

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:38.973
- I've been there-

00:10:38.973 --> 00:10:39.910
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
he wouldn't accept it.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:42.583
And he never did, and that's
happened so many times here.

00:10:42.583 --> 00:10:45.020
- You'll find many more like that.

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:46.347
It's the way we're raised, its-

00:10:46.347 --> 00:10:48.290
- [Interviewer] Whereas I'm
so used to people saying,

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.250
they'll take my money and run-

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.750
- It's the morals instilled in us.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.808
I see that a lot down in Texas.

00:10:52.808 --> 00:10:53.987
- [Interviewer] Yeah, I would think Texas

00:10:53.987 --> 00:10:57.247
has some of this too.

00:10:57.247 --> 00:11:00.360
- People is just different,
it's a different caliber here.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:04.320
- [Interviewer] Yeah, it's so
beautiful to hear your story.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.910
- Thank you, man.

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.550
It's been a long story,

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:09.690
but I don't have to look
over my shoulder anymore.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:10.942
You hear me, I'm free now-

00:11:10.942 --> 00:11:11.790
- [Interviewer] How old are you?

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:12.760
- I'm 33 years old.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:13.890
- [Interviewer] 33, you're still young.

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:14.723
- I got my whole life ahead of me.

00:11:14.723 --> 00:11:16.223
I want to become a coast guard.

00:11:17.701 --> 00:11:20.390
That's what I want to do eventually.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:22.989
Somehow I want to become a coast guard.

00:11:22.989 --> 00:11:25.390
I would even become a police
officer if they let me,

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:26.510
but they won't let me.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:28.297
Because I don't want my
son walking on the rocks

00:11:28.297 --> 00:11:29.840
that I stumbled on.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:30.890
I don't want that.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.890
I want a better life for him,

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.360
and I will do whatever it takes

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.040
to see that he has a better life.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:36.873
- [Interviewer] Were you religious

00:11:36.873 --> 00:11:38.250
before you went to prison?

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.433
- Some, but not really, no.

00:11:41.715 --> 00:11:44.300
I found God in prison.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.823
He found me, should I say.

00:11:47.659 --> 00:11:48.833
And he's real.

00:11:51.217 --> 00:11:52.460
- [Interviewer] All right, Shane.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:53.525
Thank you so much for sharing your story-

00:11:53.525 --> 00:11:54.358
- Thank you.

00:11:54.358 --> 00:11:55.381
- [Interviewer] And I
wish you the best of luck.

00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:56.610
- Thank you.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:57.443
- [Interviewer] Thank you.

00:11:57.443 --> 00:11:58.276
- I didn't mean to cry on you though.

00:11:58.276 --> 00:12:02.120
- [Interviewer] That's
all right, it's all good.

00:12:05.654 --> 00:12:07.604
- I don't have to do this no more, man.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:11.430
- [Interviewer] You had Bibles in prison?

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.380
- Yeah. They gave this to me in prison.

00:12:14.768 --> 00:12:17.297
Property of inmate Shane (indistinct).

00:12:22.461 --> 00:12:25.711
(Shane exhales deeply)

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.123
My favorite verses is right here.

